From 613a7014be907fbd23d15ff7e60fc251062b2e54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "qwen.ai[bot]" <qwenlm-intl@service.alibaba.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:12:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Replace standalone game installs with Quiver Launcher

Remove the four per-game build scripts (Daggerfall Unity, Ship of
Harkinian, 2Ship2Harkinian, SA Mod Manager installer) and install a
single Quiver Launcher AppImage instead. Quiver manages those repos
per-user via its community catalog, so the games no longer need to be
baked into the image.

Keep the Flathub packages for Nanosaur/Nanosaur 2/OpenMW/Hedge Mod
Manager/UT99/UT2004: they are sandboxed and Quiver is not a security
equivalent (no OpenMW/jorio/UT entries exist in its catalog, and UT has
no native Linux build). Add a quiver-setup justfile recipe that seeds
the user library from /etc/skel.
